SUMMARY:Space-Efficient Hierholzer (Ziad Ismaili  Alaoui)
LOCATION:LG23\, Computer Science
DESCRIPTION:Ziad Ismaili  Alaoui\nTheoretical Computer Science Seminar\n\nH
 ere is a popular challenge: Can you copy a given drawing without lifting y
 our pen or tracing any line more than once? A familiar example is the "Hau
 s vom Nikolaus" (house of Santa Claus): a square with both diagonals and a
  triangular roof. In graph-theoretic terms\, this is the same as asking fo
 r an Eulerian trail\; that is\, a walk that traverses every edge exactly o
 nce. (In this talk\, we focus on Eulerian cycles\, where the endpoints of 
 the trail are equal.) The question of finding Eulerian cycles or character
 ising which graphs have one goes back to Euler's work on the bridges of K
 önigsberg\, which many cite as the birth of graph theory. Hierholzer's al
 gorithm is a classical method for…\n\nDetails: https://researchseminars.
 org/talk/TheoryCSBham/89/
